# Time-Series Failure Prediction

Advanced time-series ML model for equipment failure forecasting, achieving 92% accuracy in industrial settings. This system prevented $1.2M in potential downtime through early failure detection.

## Architecture

![Model Architecture](docs/model_architecture.png)

The system combines LSTM networks with attention mechanisms and Transformer models to capture both short and long-term patterns in equipment sensor data. It includes uncertainty quantification to provide confidence levels with predictions.

## Key Features
- Multi-horizon forecasting with uncertainty estimation
- Advanced feature engineering for sensor data
- Temporal attention mechanisms for interpretability
- Bayesian hyperparameter optimization
- Sliding window validation approach for realistic evaluation

## Performance
The system achieves 92% accuracy in forecasting equipment failures up to 72 hours in advance, with precision and recall of 89% and 93% respectively. When deployed in a chemical processing facility, it prevented an estimated $1.2M in potential downtime costs.

